  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed a 92-minute set at Washington's in Fort Collins, Colorado, on September 14, 2018 [1]. This was the 268th show in the archive’s collection for the band, following a performance in Boulder the previous day [5]. The recommended recording, tmg2018-09-14, is a matrix mix of soundboard and audience microphones, capturing all 23 songs including five encores [1]. It was taped and transferred by LMGBTapes, and two listeners rated it five stars [1]. One reviewer described the audio as spectacular, noting that Kyle’s recordings continue to improve [3]. Another listener highlighted that the set includes a rare live version of a song where Matt adds a saxophone line, calling it one of the best recordings of that track [4]. The setlist spans albums from *The Sunset Tree* to *All Eternals Deck*, featuring tracks like “High Hawk Season” and “Moon Over Goldsboro” [1]. Rare pieces include an intro to Agnostic Front’s “Victim in Pain” and a song for Black Sabbath’s second North American tour [1]. The encore section includes “Amy aka Spent Gladiator 1” and “Up The Wolves,” the latter featuring Al Riggs [1]. The uploader thanked the sound crew and management for permission to record [1]. A second recording exists with 22 songs, but the recommended file is more complete [1][2].",
